WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.108
Open AURA and request a diagram directly, or
choose Diagram in the response format

00:00:06.108 --> 00:00:12.515
selector. Describe the components and the
direction of each interaction. Our synthetic

00:00:12.515 --> 00:00:18.474
example contains a browser, an API and
PostgreSQL. The saved document belongs to

00:00:18.474 --> 00:00:22.050
this conversation and remains a draft to
review.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:29.193
Open the document workspace, inspect labels
and use zoom or actual size to read the

00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:35.383
graph. Examine its complete outline and
source references. Supplied context means

00:00:35.383 --> 00:00:41.725
attribution to your request, not verified
infrastructure. Export SVG for a scalable

00:00:41.725 --> 00:00:47.150
diagram or PNG for a bounded image; JSON
preserves the structured data.

00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:53.577
Next request a report that separates
supplied facts, unknowns and proposed

00:00:53.577 --> 00:00:59.414
checks. Read every section and table.
Missing information must remain unknown

00:00:59.414 --> 00:01:05.479
rather than becoming an invented result.
Markdown preserves readable text, while

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:11.392
printing offers a paginated PDF. Reopen
history to recover the saved document.

00:01:12.192 --> 00:01:18.238
Prepare a memory note only when the result
is worth retaining. The form opens with an

00:01:18.238 --> 00:01:24.355
unverified summary as a question. Review the
text, choose a scope and save explicitly.

00:01:24.355 --> 00:01:30.543
Nothing is automatically written to Neo4j.
Cancel the form if the content should remain

00:01:30.543 --> 00:01:32.392
only in this conversation.
